{"_id": "26269204|None", "id": "26269204", "infons": {}, "passages": [{"infons": {"journal": "Ann Oncol. 2015 Oct;26(10):2073-8. doi: 10.1093/annonc/mdv319. Epub 2015 Aug 12.", "year": "2015", "type": "title", "authors": "Planchard D, Loriot Y, Andre F, Gobert A, Auger N, Lacroix L, Soria JC"}, "offset": 0, "text": "EGFR-independent mechanisms of acquired resistance to AZD9291 in EGFR T790M-positive NSCLC patients.", "sentences": [], "annotations": [{"id": "6", "infons": {"identifier": "1956", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "74545", "valid": true, "normalized": [1956], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 1956, "biotype": "gene", "name": "EGFR", "accession": "@GENE_EGFR"}, "text": "EGFR", "locations": [{"offset": 0, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "7", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:C000596361", "type": "Chemical", "valid": true, "normalized": ["C000596361"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "C000596361", "biotype": "chemical", "name": "osimertinib", "accession": "@CHEMICAL_osimertinib"}, "text": "AZD9291", "locations": [{"offset": 54, "length": 7}]}, {"id": "8", "infons": {"identifier": "1956", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "74545", "valid": true, "normalized": [1956], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 1956, "biotype": "gene", "name": "EGFR", "accession": "@GENE_EGFR"}, "text": "EGFR", "locations": [{"offset": 65, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "9", "infons": {"identifier": "tmVar:p|SUB|T|790|M;HGVS:p.T790M;VariantGroup:0;CorrespondingGene:1956;RS#:121434569;CorrespondingSpecies:9606;CA#:90928", "type": "Variant", "valid": true, "subtype": "ProteinMutation", "database": "litvar", "hgvs": "p.T790M", "gene_ids": [1956], "gene_id": 1956, "rsids": ["rs121434569"], "species_ids": [9606], "species_id": 9606, "clingen_id": "CA90928", "rsid": "rs121434569", "normalized": ["rs121434569##", "#1956#", "CA90928#rs121434569##"], "normalized_id": "rs121434569##", "biotype": "variant", "name": "p.T790M", "accession": "@VARIANT_p.T790M_EGFR_human"}, "text": "T790M", "locations": [{"offset": 70, "length": 5}]}, {"id": "10", "infons": {"type": "Disease", "valid": false, "normalized_id": null, "biotype": "disease"}, "text": "NSCLC", "locations": [{"offset": 85, "length": 5}]}, {"id": "11", "infons": {"identifier": "9606", "type": "Species", "valid": true, "normalized": [9606], "database": "ncbi_taxonomy", "normalized_id": 9606, "biotype": "species", "name": "9606", "accession": null}, "text": "patients", "locations": [{"offset": 91, "length": 8}]}], "relations": []}, {"infons": {"type": "abstract"}, "offset": 101, "text": "BACKGROUND: AZD9291 is an oral, irreversible, mutant-selective epidermal growth factor receptor (EGFR) tyrosine kinase inhibitors (EGFR-TKI), which specifically targets both sensitizing and resistant T790M mutations. This compound has shown outstanding activity, in a phase I/II (AURA) trial. However, despite impressive tumor responses in T790M-positive patients, acquired resistance to this drug limits the benefit of this compound. Mutations at the EGFR C797 codon, located within the kinase-binding site, were very recently reported to be a potential mechanism of resistance to AZD9291 in T790M-positive patients. PATIENTS AND METHODS: To identify potential mechanisms of resistance to AZD9291, we report here on two patients with resistant biopsy specimens that had been treated with AZD9291. RESULTS: We identified in two distinct cases, HER2 and MET amplification by FISH and CGH as a potential mechanism of acquired resistance to third-generation EGFR-TKI. Interestingly, this event occurred with complete loss of the T790M mutation. In one case, we observed a different molecular status at two biopsy sites (the T790M mutation at the primary site and wild-type T790M at the metastatic site with different pathways of acquired resistance to AZD9291). CONCLUSION: Our observations suggest that T790M-positive and wild-type T790M clones may coexist at baseline. AZD9291 efficiently suppresses the growth of T790M-positive cells, but a population of wild-type T790M cells at baseline will mediate the development of resistance, here via a by-pass pathway activating either HER2 or MET.", "sentences": [], "annotations": [{"id": "43", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:C000596361", "type": "Chemical", "valid": true, "normalized": ["C000596361"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "C000596361", "biotype": "chemical", "name": "osimertinib", "accession": "@CHEMICAL_osimertinib"}, "text": "AZD9291", "locations": [{"offset": 113, "length": 7}]}, {"id": "44", "infons": {"identifier": "1956", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "74545", "valid": true, "normalized": [1956], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 1956, "biotype": "gene", "name": "EGFR", "accession": "@GENE_EGFR"}, "text": "epidermal growth factor receptor", "locations": [{"offset": 164, "length": 32}]}, {"id": "45", "infons": {"identifier": "1956", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "74545", "valid": true, "normalized": [1956], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 1956, "biotype": "gene", "name": "EGFR", "accession": "@GENE_EGFR"}, "text": "EGFR", "locations": [{"offset": 198, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "46", "infons": {"identifier": "7294", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "2497", "valid": true, "normalized": [7294], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 7294, "biotype": "gene", "name": "TXK", "accession": "@GENE_TXK"}, "text": "tyrosine kinase", "locations": [{"offset": 204, "length": 15}]}, {"id": "47", "infons": {"identifier": "1956", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "74545", "valid": true, "normalized": [1956], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 1956, "biotype": "gene", "name": "EGFR", "accession": "@GENE_EGFR"}, "text": "EGFR", "locations": [{"offset": 232, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "48", "infons": {"identifier": "tmVar:p|SUB|T|790|M;HGVS:p.T790M;VariantGroup:0;CorrespondingGene:1956;RS#:121434569;CorrespondingSpecies:9606;CA#:90928", "type": "Variant", "valid": true, "subtype": "ProteinMutation", "database": "litv